  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, avgpool, concat) is the current best at 0.619 acc, showing that multimodal + multiprofile + avgpool is a strong combination. However, all multimodal experiments so far have used 'concat' fusion; the 'weighted' fusion strategy remains untested. Question: Does learned/weighted fusion of the two modality embeddings improve over simple concatenation in the best-performing setup? This is a single-variable change (fusion: concat→weighted) from config_018, making any performance difference cleanly attributable to the fusion mechanism. Why best next: Under a limited budget, resolving whether concat is already near-optimal or whether weighted fusion unlocks further gains is a high-information experiment. If weighted fusion helps, it opens a new optimization axis for all future multimodal configs; if it does not, we can confidently fix fusion=concat and redirect budget toward the more uncertain image-encoder (ViT-L vs ResNet50) or RNA-encoder (scvi/scgpt vs PCA) axes. It is the lowest-cost, highest-clarity test available."
}

